          "body": "tl;dr - this carries the possibility to verify any future mac arm build\n\nThat is indeed an issue. Homebrew currently does not enable codesigning correctly with builds for arm64. As do quite a few Beta 7 & Beta 8 users. Using gnu's libtool seems to be related to the issue. \n\nAs far as I see this also will affect ports.\n\nSo far the ONLY valid option to get wireshark compiled on MacOSX 11 is XCode CLT, NOT the hardcoded one. \n\nThe solution here would be to push for a change in zlib.pc not remove a valid test for a whole group of builds. If it breaks, it breaks so correctly. Fixing this just masks the breakage.\n\nTo be clear, this REALLY is an issue for me on the arm plattform. I would much rather change the script to build zlib outside of brew (which is what I do at the moment), then forcing the main CLT",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
